@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``.
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers or objects, does not wrap or crop text to the console width, does not apply markup, and does not replace emoji codes. It does support automatic highlighting (via the ``highlight`` argument, which defaults to ``True``) and a basic ``style``. Use ``out`` when you want the text written exactly as given, for example when the output contains square brackets or emoji codes that should appear literally.
+
+    >>> console.out("[bold] :smile:", "foo")
+
+
 Justify / Alignment
